      content: "Port Alder is cheaper than most of the country: a one-bedroom rents for about eleven hundred dollars a month, groceries cost a little under the national average and electricity runs close to twenty cents a kilowatt-hour. A mechanic makes about twenty-four dollars an hour and a nurse about forty-five.",
      keys: ["rent", "cost of living", "prices", "wages"],
